    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b0cbc49dd1feae00c13574ba9be36b56f3117b08d55039dd6c32c162d20dcded",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper gives a chain of representation changes for RH-sensitive zero information. For the repeated rational kernel, integration by parts turns a weighted arg zeta integral into an integral of Re(zeta'/zeta), while differentiating a parameterized log|zeta| identity reaches the same log-derivative interface and differentiates its off-line-zero corrections. Independently, the counting function turns a weighted sum over zero ordinates into an arg-zeta integral by Stieltjes integration, and the antiderivative S1 together with Littlewood's theorem turns that phase integral into a half-plane log-modulus integral; this is why the Volchkov and Balazard-Saias-Yor formulations are rewritings rather than independent evidence. Multiplying zeta(z) by z-1 supplies a related pole-regularized modulus representation whose contour residues retain explicit, one-signed sensitivity to off-line zeros.",
      "parent_sources": [
